        <p class="lead text-ink-soft mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
          From our executive team to directors and branch presidents across Loudoun County. Hover to pause, tap any card to read their story, or use the arrows to browse.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Marquee: full-bleed strip that auto-scrolls slowly. Two identical
           copies of the roster are laid end to end so the scroll loops
           seamlessly. Auto-scroll pauses on hover/focus (so a card can be
           flipped) and while the visitor is browsing; the arrow buttons jump a
           few members at a time, and native touch/trackpad swiping works too.
           Under prefers-reduced-motion the auto-scroll never starts - the arrows
           and swiping still do. Behaviour lives in the script below.

           The duplicate copy is hidden from assistive tech and dropped from the
           tab order, but it must stay clickable: for most of the loop the strip
           on screen is largely made of duplicate cards, so making that copy
           inert (as it once was) left the visible cards dead to hover and
           clicks until the drift wrapped around. Cards flip in pairs by
           data-flip-key, so the copies never disagree. -->
      <div class="marquee group mt-12" data-marquee>
